# TEMPLATE: a wish worn on the knight (gear: a shield, a helm, pauldrons, boots).
# Copy this file, then change what it says. Check it with
#   cargo run -p angel-delve --example content_check -- <your file>
# and add the entry to cockpit/assets/dungeon/phrasebook.txt when it passes.
#
# Change: the id (lowercase-with-dashes, at most 24), the Name (at most 18, the
#   player's words), every `say` (the player's words first, then 3 to 6 other
#   ways), the effect words and their numbers, the scroll lines after `::`,
#   the picture and its place (`at=`: head 10x8, face 8x4, body 12x6,
#   shoulders 16x5, back 14x10, left 8x12, right 8x16, feet 12x3).
# Keep: five tiers, each giving more than the one below once the game's caps
#   apply (a word wishes cap, like armor 2, climbs to its cap by the third tier,
#   then the fourth and fifth add another word beside it); the look drawn at its
#   place's size or smaller (bigger is squeezed to fit and loses pixels); the
#   card art 12 to 14 rows.
# The bar: every picture Fine or better (Masterwork for a template): one clear
#   silhouette, an edge darker than its inside, 4 to 6 inks shaded dark to
#   light, one accent, no specks. Each `say` finds this wish and no other.
wish spiked-pavise | Spiked Pavise
say a spiked shield | spiked pavise | tower shield | bigger shield | heavier shield
tier armor 1 :: A spiked pavise: 6 in the hundred of every hit turned aside.
tier armor 2 :: A heavier pavise: 11 in the hundred turned aside.
tier armor 2; max_hp 15 :: A great pavise: 11 in the hundred, and 15 more health.
tier armor 2; max_hp 25 :: A mighty pavise: 11 in the hundred, and 25 more health.
tier armor 2; max_hp 35; knock 1 :: The full pavise: 11 aside, 35 health, and it shoves.
draw worn at=left
